%N A208849 Number of Josephus subsets of n people.
%C A208849 A Josephus subset is a subset of people in the Josephus problem of a circle of n people for which some positive integer k exists which removes all those not in the subset first, by starting the count at person 1 and removing every k-th person clockwise.
%H A208849 <a href="/index/J#Josephus">Index entries for sequences related to the Josephus Problem</a>
%F A208849 a(n) = 2^n - A208848(n).
